  "changes": [
    "Map2 player-owned3032/3186/3250/6197011/6197021/6197031/6197041/6197501 missiles continue after first contact, turn and return to current owner position",
    "Same native type8 entity/prefab/ID retained; native rotateTo and moveTo events plus stored snapshot angle/position updated",
    "One contact per target life per leg; swept outbound and inbound segments, including both legs in a long frame",
    "Death/scene/source world or actor/room/map change cancels; owner catch, return-distance budget and wall-clock TTL delete native visibility row",
    "Frozen-segment persistence retry keeps already settled target markers and retries only unsettled hits; kill/XP once",
    "Big boomerang3186 now scheduled with native150ms castPointTime and one stamina charge; scheduled active profile coverage grows13 to14",
    "Two prior tests updated: native RMB test waits actual windup/world tick; native scheduled-profile count/path test includes3186"
  ],
  "policies": {
    "evidence": "Original native IDs/speed/range/skillSize/prefab paths used. English3186 description specifies two hits;3252 describes basic projectile damage on return. Ordinary3032 return inferred from native boomerang family/name. Client descriptions are not complete original server algorithms.",
    "trajectory": "Straight outbound to full native maxDistance, then home toward current owner at native skillSpeed, recomputing direction each segment. Not enemy homing. Cursor affects initial release only; return follows owner. No turn hold from SkillScheme.duration and no recovered curved retail easing. Active3186 currently uses full native range along cursor axis, not a separately reconstructed target-point stopping rule.",
    "contacts": "Each target record+spawnToken can be damaged once outbound and once inbound. Both legs can settle in one world frame at a close turn. Same native attack definition/crit/resistance/reward path used per hit. Return pierces all eligible contacts; this per-leg/pierce/turn-overlap policy is local. Resources/chests/statues remain eligible like prior generic missiles; protected/hidden/dead/depleted targets excluded.",
    "incompleteGhost": "Ghost Shadow args.interval/extDmgInterval and enhanced extra tick behavior NOT restored. The new per-leg contact rule is not claimed exact retail timing. Boomerang legacy selfBuffArgs/control effects also not fully restored.",
    "terrain": "Existing ordinary projectile terrain behavior retained: these returning missiles do not gain a new wall/terrain ray blocker. Safe target areas still exclude damage on either leg. Correct retail terrain/return interaction remains unverified; Stage44 wall data/code untouched.",
    "lifetime": "Attach only to player-owned matching skills in Map2; companion actors and other maps retain prior behavior. Already flying missile survives weapon change. Cancel on invalid source scene/world/entity/HP/room/map. Same-map relocation can change return destination. Return budget=2*maxDistance; wall TTL=max(5000,3*maxDistance/speed*1000+3000)ms. Caps and cancellation are local safety/lifecycle policies, not native TTL values.",
    "retry": "Failed lethal reward persistence freezes current swept segment and its target list; successfully settled targets marked only after success. Retry after250ms, warning at most once per5000ms; skips dead/replaced target lives. Pending segment committed without duplicate earlier damage; TTL can end permanent failures without fake reward. Frozen contacts may settle against their original attempted segment after target movement; reconstructed policy.",
    "delivery": "Existing environment row persists for both legs; final unregister plus normal destroy/recovery queue. Updating ud.angle affects late snapshots; rotateTo drives existing native transformer. No general texture/UI/backpressure recovery guarantee.",
    "validation": "Native SkillCfg/PathUtil/SkillResUtil executed for all8 IDs; original CCAsyncBulletEntity.transform forwards rotateTo; three original imports CRC/hash verified. No Windows renderer/live client. Active scheduler latency uses existing50ms timer and other native salvo lifecycle policies."
  },
